{%- comment -%}
  What js/link-preview.js shows when a reader holds still over a link to
  somewhere else on the site: the title, what kind of thing it is, and the
  sentence the page already uses to describe itself. No bodies — those are
  what make the search index large, and this one is fetched because somebody
  paused, not because they asked for anything.

  Same records and the same order as /search-index.json, from the same
  include, so a section cannot be in one and missing from the other.
{%- endcomment -%}
